--
-- Version control: branches isolate data.  Each branch keeps its own
-- working set; checking out another branch shows that branch's rows, and
-- coming back shows this branch's uncommitted changes again.
--
\set ECHO none
commit base|t
create branch|t
checkout feature|t
feature rows|1:changed,2:feature
checkout main|t
main rows|1:base
back to feature|t
feature rows kept|1:changed,2:feature
commit feature|t
checkout main again|t
main rows kept|1:base,3:main
commit main|t
branch from commit|t
checkout old|t
old rows|1:base
after rollback|1
ERROR:  branch "vb_no_such_branch" does not exist
back to main|t
